{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/920930-cross-line-play-with-minor-templates","id":920930,"title":"Cross-line play with Minor Templates","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-25T06:17:35-07:00","id":920930,"title":"Cross-line play with Minor Templates","content":"Hey all, <br /> <br /> I've had a game idea rattling around for the last week or so, and it coalesced this morning into a pitch I gave my players:<br /> <br /> Chronicles of Darkness police procedural. You're a cross-section of the local police force, who end up encountering the supernatural and getting thrown together. You also all have a secret - Maybe you're a dirty cop, maybe you're addicted to something etc. Your job will be to deal with the supernatural, while keeping your secret safe. <br /> <br /> What I've not mentioned is that the secret is that they're all different flavours of supernatural. Maybe they've got Biokinesis, maybe they're a Stigmatic, or maybe they're a Wolf-Blooded. I'm aiming to introduce some group conflict (In a pleasant way - Everyone works really well together, so this should provide some tension without actually causing problems). <br /> <br /> <i>As best as I can tell,</i> most of the minor templates really are quite minor. Wolf-Blooded buys you a 3-merit Tell (And I'll strongly encourage the ones that play well outside of the Pack), Sleepwalker seems easy, Stigmatic seems straight-forward (It's basically the generic supernatural merits, plus a bit of God-Machine flavour)<br /> <br /> The ones that concern me are Ghouls - They seem relatively powerful. They're a full-on Supernatural force, rather than just Human+. <br /> <br /> I'm also not sure whether Hunters can be counted as a minor template or not, if they're not too well connected to the bigger groups. I'll need to go through their book and check them out, especially in the context of 2nd ed and Mortal Remains.<br /> <br /> I'm not familiar with the other minor templates. I know there's a preview for Fae Touched, but I'm not sure how much that's going to match the final version. Are the children of Demons a minor template, or are they just Demons with less connection to the God-Machine? <br /> <br /> Thoughts? Anyone managed something like this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T09:57:51-07:00","id":921003,"title":"","content":"The Hurt Locker previews include some really cool minor templates you could use. They range a lot in power depending on how many merit dots you sink into them, but that's a pretty easy scale to adjust.<br /> <br /> Lost Boys are my favorite of the lot, super soldiers dependent on regular serum doses to keep their bodies from rejecting the implants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T10:31:08-07:00","id":921017,"title":"","content":"Yes, my vampire game started as a minor template one, with hunters.<br /> <br /> Ghouls do have the capacity to be very powerful, but they're also one of the few that must maintain a link to their corresponding major template.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T10:43:08-07:00","id":921023,"title":"","content":"Ooh, the Lost Boys are very interesting.<br /> <br /> Probably a bit more militaristic than I was looking for this campaign (If more than 1 character even has regular access to a gun, something has gone very, very weird) but it's definitely an option. Maybe go with a God-Machine tie in, to make it more weirdly supernatural. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T12:32:40-07:00","id":921089,"title":"","content":"Fractals are also pretty up there on the power spectrum for minor templates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T12:40:33-07:00","id":921092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/920930-cross-line-play-with-minor-templates?p=921089#post921089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fractals are also pretty up there on the power spectrum for minor templates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely think I'll have to rule them out - I just found the wiki page, and I don't see how you can have one of them in the party without the game being about them personally. <br /> <br /> Offspring seem much more reasonable though (Although I suppose it depends on how exactly they work)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T12:59:37-07:00","id":921103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/920930-cross-line-play-with-minor-templates?p=921092#post921092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely think I'll have to rule them out - I just found the wiki page, and I don't see how you can have one of them in the party without the game being about them personally.<br /> <br /> Offspring seem much more reasonable though (Although I suppose it depends on how exactly they work)</div> </div> </div> </div>Fractals start with more Embeds and interlocks, but both types can learn Embeds at the normal cost (2xp each). Fractals are the only ones that gain the ability to see through Cover, and there's a merit that allows them to detect demonic lies.<br /> <br /> Both types are considered stigmatics, so can acquire the full suite of supernatural merits. They're basically 'Stigmatic+' instead of 'Human+'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T13:04:48-07:00","id":921108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/920930-cross-line-play-with-minor-templates?p=921103#post921103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fractals start with more Embeds and interlocks, but both types can learn Embeds at the normal cost (2xp each). Fractals are the only ones that gain the ability to see through Cover, and there's a merit that allows them to detect demonic lies.<br /> <br /> Both types are considered stigmatics, so can acquire the full suite of supernatural merits. They're basically 'Stigmatic+' instead of 'Human+'</div> </div> </div> </div>That is definitely a shame. They seem really interesting, but I'm pitching this game over my original idea for Demon as it is. I'm going to have to walk a fine-line for it not to feel bait and switchy, and &quot;Baby Demons with access to a decent chunk of the Demon powers&quot; might be a bit much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T14:43:36-07:00","id":921173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/920930-cross-line-play-with-minor-templates?p=921103#post921103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fractals start with more Embeds and interlocks, but both types can learn Embeds at the normal cost (2xp each). Fractals are the only ones that gain the ability to see through Cover, and there's a merit that allows them to detect demonic lies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not entirely correct. As far as I know, fractals can only see through the covers of their parents. Also, according to page 30 of Heirs to Hell, Embeds cost 4 xp each for demon-blooded characters.<br /> <br /> I currently have one Fractal in my mortal++ campaign, and although she has stronger supernatural powers than most other players, I make sure she doesn't overshadow other players by restricting the Embeds she may buy. But I would recommend against having demon-blooded characters in campaigns that do not feature the God-Machine, as most downsides of the template key off the God-Machine, and the template is meant to reinforce the themes of a Demon (or at least God-Machine) game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T15:11:57-07:00","id":921188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/920930-cross-line-play-with-minor-templates?p=921103#post921103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fractals start with more Embeds and interlocks, but both types can learn Embeds at the normal cost (2xp each). Fractals are the only ones that gain the ability to see through Cover, and there's a merit that allows them to detect demonic lies.<br /> <br /> Both types are considered stigmatics, so can acquire the full suite of supernatural merits. They're basically 'Stigmatic+' instead of 'Human+'</div> </div> </div> </div>Fractals can also store Aether, as opposed to being forced to use Ambient Aether.<br /> <br /> If you put limits on what Embeds are allowed to be acquired and when, Offspring are very manageable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/920930-cross-line-play-with-minor-templates?p=921108#post921108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is definitely a shame. They seem really interesting, but I'm pitching this game over my original idea for Demon as it is. I'm going to have to walk a fine-line for it not to feel bait and switchy, and &quot;Baby Demons with access to a decent chunk of the Demon powers&quot; might be a bit much.</div> </div> </div> </div>That title actually belongs to Nephilim, who even track Primum stat. <hr /><br /> I'm working on project for a Mortal+ level minor template (micro is more like - it is literally one Merit that only lets you access a system, that's <i>all</i>) - Hedge Sorcerers. Basically, they're mortals with a deal with the Wyrd to use Contracts (from Changeling 2E - you can see a decent amount from the playtest preview). Contracts are priced as Merits (1XP per Dot), and since Hedge Sorcerers lack Glamour, they need to use the Catches, but other than that, it seems to work fine. Players/Characters might need to do some additional social/environmental engineering to employ their powers, but that just helps the flavor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-25-2016, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T11:22:15-07:00","id":922109,"title":"","content":"Fae Touched are more powerful then ghouls for couple of reasons.<br /> <br /> 1 they can harvest their own glamour via emotions, even without Changeling support, Ghoul need to be given vitae from a vampire.<br /> <br /> 2 Touch Fae have access to all kinds of contracts, admittedly they need a Changeling to train them,aside from their 2 free dots. Ghouls I believe can't take Coils of the Dragon, use any disciplines that require bleeding out vitae.<br /> <br /> 3 With a merit they can gain a mask/mien which they can drop to bewitch people and get autosuccesses on contracts.<br /> <br /> 4. They can also get the Seeming effects of their Seeming on contracts.<br /> <br /> 5. They can do Sealings and join Changeling Courts for extra bonuses.<br /> <br /> I can build an Elemental Fae Touched character with 12xp that has both Armour of the Phantom Glory contract with elemental effect, and Stealing the Solid Reflection contract with elemental effect.<br /> <br /> So the Fae Touched character can drop their mask, turn into fire, making her invulnerible to physical attacks, and allowing her to deal lethal fire damage, then pull a copy of herself out of a nearby reflection, and attack any equal xp ghoul and kill it with ease. Actually that would likely be enough to kill many vampires.<br /> <br /> In the unlikely event that things go heywire, that Fae Touched can just go into twilight and be invisible, or pull the reflection of a car out and drive away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T13:55:51-07:00","id":922203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/920930-cross-line-play-with-minor-templates?p=922109#post922109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fae Touched are more powerful then ghouls for couple of reasons.<br /> <br /> 1 they can harvest their own glamour via emotions, even without Changeling support, Ghoul need to be given vitae from a vampire.<br /> <br /> 2 Touch Fae have access to all kinds of contracts, admittedly they need a Changeling to train them,aside from their 2 free dots. Ghouls I believe can't take Coils of the Dragon, use any disciplines that require bleeding out vitae.<br /> <br /> 3 With a merit they can gain a mask/mien which they can drop to bewitch people and get autosuccesses on contracts.<br /> <br /> 4. They can also get the Seeming effects of their Seeming on contracts.<br /> <br /> 5. They can do Sealings and join Changeling Courts for extra bonuses.<br /> <br /> I can build an Elemental Fae Touched character with 12xp that has both Armour of the Phantom Glory contract with elemental effect, and Stealing the Solid Reflection contract with elemental effect.<br /> <br /> So the Fae Touched character can drop their mask, turn into fire, making her invulnerible to physical attacks, and allowing her to deal lethal fire damage, then pull a copy of herself out of a nearby reflection, and attack any equal xp ghoul and kill it with ease. Actually that would likely be enough to kill many vampires.<br /> <br /> In the unlikely event that things go heywire, that Fae Touched can just go into twilight and be invisible, or pull the reflection of a car out and drive away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that Fae-Touched aren't officially out yet, I think ghouls still win. Plus, your build doesn't work in the spoiled rules as written: Stealing the Solid Reflection caps traits at the user's Wyrd, which is 0, meaning your copy appears...then falls over dead. Even if it did work, it would take five rounds to get all that off (1 Glamour/round, because Wyrd 0, and fae-touched can't use catches). Maybe she can survive 2-3 rounds before Phantom Glory kicks in, maybe not, but it's not exactly the bulldoze that you imply. (Don't drive in reflected cars, kids: the driver's door will be on the right side, and your gas and break will be switched!)<br /> <br /> <br /> To answer OP's question, ghouls do get more neat power than most microtemplates. However, they also don't tend to have a lot of Vitae to play with, meaning that they have a lot of options, but not a lot of fuel. If you think the ghouls are too cool, limit their Vitae intake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T19:37:16-07:00","id":922374,"title":"","content":"Dang your right. Okay replace Solid Reflection with control elements, 1 dot of Armour of the Elements and Pathfinder.<br /> <br /> I will admit activation time is the weak point, because of the 1 glamour per turn, but if the Fae Touched can survive long enough to use Phantom Glory, the Ghoul's dead meat. <br /> <br /> The Ghouls advantages are the strong passive effects of their discplines, spending vitae to heal.<br /> <br /> The FaeTouched's strengths are potentially really powerful contract effects, Sealings, and that they can harvest their own fuel stat pretty easily.<br /> <br /> A Fae Touched Darkling with Paralyasing Shudder can basically lock the Ghoul down and cause a breaking point. This could drive the Ghoul insane. Some points in Mantle are important if one uses dropping the mask first.<br /> <br /> Other Seeming Fae Touched have their own cool tricks.<br /> <br /> And yets be honest Phantom Glory with the Elemental Effect is basically a superhero kit in of its itself. Effective invisiblity and the ability to pass through walls, and see ghosts with the basic verison, check, turn into the human torch minus the flying, but gain immunity to physical damage instead , +2 elemental damage with your touch, and the ability to pass through walls, with the elemental effect check.<br /> <br /> If you have Dark Eras, a Darkling Fae Touched can use the contract the contracts of Air and Darkness to create some truely horrifying and/or confusing illusions (although a Ghoul with nightmare can return the favour).<br /> <br /> Imagine feeling flames burning your flesh, copies of the Fae Touched so you don't know which is the real one, or the Ghouls Master, or simply having a bag over your head, amoung others.<br /> <br /> and so many other combos.<br /> <br /> I don't think Fae Touched will change in any major way, except that they probably will get rid of the earily death weakness.<br /> <br /> Iron, Madness, Hedge addiction and the other stuff is likely to be more then enough downside to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T20:18:26-07:00","id":922397,"title":"","content":"Alchemists seem to be looking pretty interesting antagonists for Promethean 2E, and while devs have stated it's not intended for players, it'd be pretty easy to adapt them for players. What they do is they can learn to replicate Distillations with alchemy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T09:03:27-07:00","id":922671,"title":"","content":"Are you planning on any other supernaturals of any description being present on the force, that <i>aren't</i> the players?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 06-28-2016, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T09:59:11-07:00","id":922701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/920930-cross-line-play-with-minor-templates?p=922671#post922671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you planning on any other supernaturals of any description being present on the force, that <i>aren't</i> the players?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've not even started thinking about the wider police force. Partly because this is set in the future of the game I'm currently running - The fate of the police force is still in flux. There's a good chance that it's about to face a purge, because there's a pissed off set of vampires who want it under their control. <br /> <br /> And partly (and more honestly) because I'm in the early stages of planning, and I'm building from who the players are. It's definitely an interesting question. I'm tempted to say yes, and go with a city that's heavy on Stigmatics, Mystery Cults (that fits the theme of the game I'm going for) and Wolf-Blooded (Which is something I've not had chance to bring into it much yet). The state of the Ghouls depends on their actions in this game. <br /> <br /> There's not going to be a very high intensity though. I see it more as having lots of low-level freakiness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T10:33:02-07:00","id":922715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/920930-cross-line-play-with-minor-templates?p=922701#post922701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've not even started thinking about the wider police force. And partly (and more honestly) because I'm in the early stages of planning, and I'm building from who the players are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both fair points. <br /> <br /> Also, Spike Men. Nice and grounded and down-to-earth, comparatively. Just get 'em past the physical.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T07:34:27-07:00","id":924443,"title":"","content":"Oh, I just remembered: if you don't mind making some on the spot conversions (between 1E material and 2E), you could even let a Witness pick up Affinities. There's some discussion <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/914948-soul-and-word-mortal-mummy-magic\">here</a> on that. You could either use Risen Pillars as listed, or go with the other potential version <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/914948-soul-and-word-mortal-mummy-magic?p=922731#post922731\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> So if you wanted an officer with an extra-special bond with their K-9 partner, have them take Risen Pillar (Ba) \u2022, then pick up the Beast Companion Affinity. Roughly 4XP (7XP if you require them to be a Witness first) for an amazing duo (and canines benefit from the Sacred Animal effect, so they'd even heal like a Mummy!).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-01-2016, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T11:53:34-07:00","id":924555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/920930-cross-line-play-with-minor-templates?p=924443#post924443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I just remembered: if you don't mind making some on the spot conversions (between 1E material and 2E), you could even let a Witness pick up Affinities. There's some discussion <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/914948-soul-and-word-mortal-mummy-magic\">here</a> on that. You could either use Risen Pillars as listed, or go with the other potential version <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/914948-soul-and-word-mortal-mummy-magic?p=922731#post922731\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> So if you wanted an officer with an extra-special bond with their K-9 partner, have them take Risen Pillar (Ba) \u2022, then pick up the Beast Companion Affinity. Roughly 4XP (7XP if you require them to be a Witness first) for an amazing duo (and canines benefit from the Sacred Animal effect, so they'd even heal like a Mummy!).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really useful, thanks. <br /> <br /> Are there any other good animal-companion minor templates? The Police Dog handler was one role I was a bit unsure of how to support. Ghoul with Animalism 1 can do a bit of it. Wolfblooded can manage it a little, with one of their Tells. Do the Fae-touched get any sort of animal connection?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T12:17:05-07:00","id":924559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/920930-cross-line-play-with-minor-templates?p=924555#post924555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's really useful, thanks.<br /> <br /> Are there any other good animal-companion minor templates? The Police Dog handler was one role I was a bit unsure of how to support. Ghoul with Animalism 1 can do a bit of it. Wolfblooded can manage it a little, with one of their Tells. Do the Fae-touched get any sort of animal connection?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hedgebeast Companion? Not pure animal, but close enough? I think there are Contracts with animal influence as well (which either a Fae-touched or Hedge Sorcerer could take). A Demon-Blooded can take Animal Communication and Animal Messenger Embeds.<br /> <br /> Yeah. <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pipes of the Beastcaller (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span>. It lets you call animals in Wyrd miles and communicate with them. Beast-effect establishes an empathic link.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":".  Found the Contract. 07-01-2016, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T12:44:10-07:00","id":924570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/920930-cross-line-play-with-minor-templates?p=924559#post924559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hedgebeast Companion? Not pure animal, but close enough? I think there are Contracts with animal influence as well (which either a Fae-touched or Hedge Sorcerer could take). A Demon-Blooded can take Animal Communication and Animal Messenger Embeds.<br /> <br /> Yeah. <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pipes of the Beastcaller (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span>. It lets you call animals in Wyrd miles and communicate with them. Beast-effect establishes an empathic link.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually I think what Hedge Beast Companions in 2e can be alot more flexible in then in 1e.<br /> <br /> In 1e they were just talking beasts, in 2e they use the stats of the closest animal type to them, which suggests they can be alot weirder, like a small none flying dragon could be represented by a big cat.<br /> <br /> Or a humaniod squirrell could be well represented by the Chimpanzee stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T12:55:11-07:00","id":924573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/920930-cross-line-play-with-minor-templates?p=924570#post924570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually I think what Hedge Beast Companions in 2e can be alot more flexible in then in 1e.<br /> <br /> In 1e they were just talking beasts, in 2e they use the stats of the closest animal type to them, which suggests they can be alot weirder, like a small none flying dragon could be represented by a big cat.<br /> <br /> Or a humaniod squirrell could be well represented by the Chimpanzee stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or a white rabbit with a punctuality obsession?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T22:09:30-07:00","id":924774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/920930-cross-line-play-with-minor-templates?p=924573#post924573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or a white rabbit with a punctuality obsession?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, I'd give a more detailed response, but I'm already late! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}